  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis is the third slice of the HEIDENHAIN Klartext reader in `camcraft-gcode` (#2227). The reader now reads the contour elements that a hand-written or other-CAM program uses most:\n\n- `RND R<r> [F<f>]` (rounding arc) and `CHF <l> [F<f>]` (chamfer) between two straight feed lines (`L` or `LP`) in the working plane. The reader looks one block ahead. A line that an `RND` / `CHF` follows waits. The line after the transition sets the cut-back points. The toolpath then gets the shortened line, the transition element and the next line. A transition that takes exactly the whole line leaves no line: the reader writes no zero-length feed move. The corner point is not machined. The rounding arc is tangent to both lines, with the tangent length R tan(phi/2). The chamfer cuts the side length from each line. The `F` of the transition acts only on the transition.\n- `LP PR.. PA.. [Z..] F../FMAX` with `IPR` / `IPA`: a straight line to polar coordinates about the pole `CC`. A polar coordinate that is not written, and the base of `IPR` / `IPA`, is the last programmed `PR` / `PA` about the current pole. The reader keeps that value only while it knows it exactly: after an `LP` (or a `CP`) about the same pole, with no X/Y move by another block and no move of the pole. When the reader does not know the value, it refuses the `LP` by name and line, for example \"LP without PR: the last polar radius about this pole is not known (write PR)\". The same rule applies to `PA`.\n- `CP PA.. DR±` and `CP IPA.. DR±`, with `Z` / `IZ` as a helix. The reader splits each `CP` into pieces of at most 90 degrees on the same circle, with Z linear over the sweep.\n\nThe reader refuses by name, line and block number what it cannot show exactly:\n\n- a transition next to an arc, a cycle, the program start or end, an `FMAX` line, a line with a Z change, a line with a block-end M function (before) or any M function (after);\n- a transition that needs more of a line than the line has (also after an earlier cut-back), and two lines in line;\n- `CP` with `IPA` and `DR` of different signs, `CP PA` at the start angle, `CP` from the pole, an `LP` whose last programmed `PR` or `PA` is not known (after a Cartesian move or a moved `CC`), an `LP` angle out of range;\n- `RL` / `RR` (the message now says why: the tool radius of the tool table and the corner rules of the control are not in the program), `APPR` / `DEP`, `CTP`, `LBL` / `CALL LBL` and inch programs stay refused.\n\nThe decisions are in `docs/decisions/2227-klartext-reader.md`, section \"third slice\".\n\nNew files: `crates/gcode/src/klartext/corner.rs`, `crates/gcode/src/klartext/polar.rs`, and the test modules `crates/gcode/tests/klartext/contours.rs` and `crates/gcode/tests/klartext/polar.rs` in the existing `klartext` directory suite (no new test binary).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nAll in the `klartext` suite of `camcraft-gcode`:\n\n- `klartext_rnd_rounds_a_right_angle_with_its_own_feed` (cut-back points, arc centre, the F of RND only on the arc, line map)\n- `klartext_chf_and_rnd_chain_on_right_turns` (chamfer, then a rounding on the shortened line, clockwise)\n- `klartext_rnd_on_an_obtuse_corner_is_tangent_to_both_lines` (radius and tangency at both ends)\n- `klartext_rnd_between_l_and_lp_lines`\n- `klartext_rnd_on_the_first_move_of_a_section_starts_at_the_line_start`\n- `klartext_transition_elements_refuse_what_is_not_exact`\n- `klartext_lp_reaches_polar_points_about_the_pole`\n- `klartext_cp_arcs_about_the_pole_in_both_directions` (also `CT` after `CP`)\n- `klartext_cp_with_iz_is_a_helix_split_into_quarter_turns`\n- `klartext_polar_blocks_refuse_what_is_not_exact`\n- `klartext_lp_refuses_a_polar_coordinate_that_it_does_not_know` (new: after a Cartesian `L`, a `C` arc or a moved `CC`; `IPR` / `IPA` without a known base)\n- `klartext_lp_keeps_the_last_polar_coordinates_where_they_are_known` (new: a Z-only move, the same `CC` again, an M block; `CP` keeps `PR`; `CP PA` sets `PA`; `CP IPA` from an unknown angle; `LP PR+0`)\n- `klartext_lp_angle_out_of_range_is_refused` (new)\n- `klartext_transition_that_takes_the_whole_line_leaves_no_zero_length_move` (new: `CHF` that takes the line before, `CHF` that takes the line after, `RND` that takes both)\n- `klartext_rnd_after_a_line_with_m3_or_m8` (new)\n- `klartext_chf_between_an_l_and_an_lp_line` (new)\n- `klartext_transition_with_fmax_is_refused` (new)\n- `klartext_contour_with_every_slice_3_element_parses`\n- `klartext_seeded_mutations_of_the_contour_never_panic` and the truncation test `klartext_every_truncation_of_the_golden_is_refused_without_a_panic`, now also over the contour program\n- `klartext_functions_outside_the_slice_are_refused_by_name_and_block` (updated: `CTP` and `RL` in `LP` replace the `LP` / `CP` rows)\n\n## Gate\n\nPre-review fixes on top of `3c24051af` (commits `55386f6bd` and `755d7dce2`). All results are on the final head `755d7dce2`, on the winbuild lane (`lanes --branch`, `--needs gcode`), in one lane run. Log `gate-4468-755d7dc.log`.\n\n- Quick gate, `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (`main` at `2394b5a`): 3 steps, 0 failed. `gcode build`, `gcode suites: lib` and `gcode suites: klartext` are ok.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-gcode --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-gcode --test klartext`: 54 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored. Each pinning test above is named in the output.\n- The first run on `55386f6bd` had one red test: `klartext_lp_keeps_the_last_polar_coordinates_where_they_are_known`. The test read a move by its index, but an `LP` that ends at the tool position adds no move. Commit `755d7dce2` corrects the test. The reader code did not change.\n- Light lane: not run. The diff is only in `camcraft-gcode`, and no light twin covers it. P7: no heavy step.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No comparison against a real control. Our sources do not say what the control keeps as the last `PR` / `PA` after a Cartesian move or a moved `CC`. The reader refuses those cases. It does not guess.\n- No comparison against a real control for the geometry either. The geometry comes from the published manual behaviour and plane geometry.\n- A transition next to an arc, `CTP`, `APPR` / `DEP`, `RL` / `RR`, `LBL` / `CALL LBL` and inch programs are refused, not read. They stay open on #2227.\n- No consumer of the reader changes. The example catalog suites do not apply: no post and no toolpath generator changed.\n\nChangelog: The Klartext reader reads RND and CHF between straight lines, polar LP and CP about CC, and the CP helix; it refuses by name what it cannot show exactly.\n\nEffort: max\n\nRefs #2227\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n",
